2 CONT Villanueva de Cavazos, Lilia E. '''''Testamentos Coloniales de Monterrey''''', Monterrey, Nuevo León, Mexico, 1991, pages 18-22. [Ramo Civil, Vol. 5, Exp. 22, Folio 3]   ...  The '''1643 will of Capitán Miguel De Montemayor'''  (d
2 CONC ated 11 October 1643) cites his parents, his wife '''Mónica Rodríguez''', her parents Capitán Diego Rodríguez and Sebastiana de Tremiño, a deceased son Lucas, as well as his legitimate children Diego, Margarita, Petrona, María, Fr
2 CONC ancisco, Domingo, José, Bernardo, and Mateo.  Additionally, the will cites two "bastard" daughters: María, wife of Juan Maldonado, and Juana, wife of Andrés de Charles.  Further, the will directs that he be interred in Monterrey's
2 CONC  Iglesia Parroquial and states that he is ill near to death.
2 CONT
2 CONT ________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Cavazos Garza, Israel. '''''Catálogo y Síntesis de los Protocolos del Archivo Municipal de Monterrey 1599-1700''''', Instituto Tecnologico y de Estudios Superiores de Monterrey, Monterrey, Nuevo León, México, 1966, page 276, #790 
2 CONC [XVIII, exp. 8, fol. 2 v].  ...  This protocolo describes the '''dowry''' of Capitán Miguel De Montemayor's marriage contract with '''Mónica Rodríguez''', citing her parents, and is dated twice--'''Villa de Cerralvo, 20 February 1
2 CONC 628''', and '''Monterrey, 19 August 1636'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Cavazos Garza, Israel. '''''Catálogo y Síntesis de los Protocolos del Archivo Municipal de Monterrey 1599-1700''''', Instituto Tecnologico y de Estudios Superiores de Monterrey, Monterrey, Nuevo León, México, 1966, pages 277-278, 
2 CONC #792 [XVIII, exp. 8, fol. 23 v].  ...  This protocolo is the '''will of Mónica Rodríguez''' and cites her parents and her directive to be buried in the Parroquial with her deceased husband,  After several religious instructions, h
2 CONC er debts are set forth, and her children listed with bequests.  Signed '''Hacienda de los Nogales, Monterrey, 18 April 1671'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT A '''second will''' is cited in a protocolo on pages 278-279, #793 [XVIII, exp. 8, fol. 33], and signed '''Hacienda de Santa Bárbara (de los Nogales), Monterrey, 19 April 1680'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________________________
